Kompakt: a2grey lifts the A2 bit depth to 4

Mudita's meink sets the bit depth only in setWaveformType, from a table
by type (A2 = 1), and its MeinkSetBpp is a no-op, so pixelbits writes
never took and Fast was always 1 bpp: the grey transitions a2grey adds
to the A2 record never saw a grey pixel. The loader's set-waveform hook
now writes 4 into the display's bpp field after an A2 upload that
carries the a2grey record. uploadImageToDisplay reads that field for
both the packing and the depth byte it sends the panel, and the refresh
mode byte does not depend on depth, so the frame goes out as the GL16
data path with the A2 LUT. Turning a2grey off re-uploads and meink's
table restores 1 bpp. Experiment; notes in the private study.

--- a/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
@@ -816,6 +816,7 @@
 #define WF_DISP_VT        0x08
 #define WF_DISP_API_MUTEX 0x10
 #define WF_DISP_WAVEFORM  0x90
+#define WF_DISP_BPP       0xa8            /* meink sets it from the waveform; pixelbits writes are a no-op */
 #define WF_MEINK_OPEN     0x4c
 
 #define WF_GU16           0x1
@@ -1038,6 +1039,10 @@
     unsigned int done = READ_ONCE(wf_done[idx]);
     const u8 *rec = wf_live + idx * WF_REC;
 
+    /* Kompakt: a2grey needs grey input, and meink pairs A2 with 1 bpp; lift it to 4, the GL16 data path. */
+    if (ret == 0 && group == WF_A2 && (done & WF_A2GREY))
+        WRITE_ONCE(*(u32 *)((u8 *)display + WF_DISP_BPP), 4);
+
     /* crc and length match the lutd= field of refresh_time when this record went out */
     pr_info("kompakt-wf: upload %s band %u N=%u crc=%08x/%u%s%s%s%s\n", wf_name[group],
             idx % WF_BANDS, rec[0], crc32_le(0, rec, rec[0] * WF_FRAME + 0x41),
